 ViewpointAudit g_vp_audit;
 
+// ── How much unobserved space a line of sight may cross ────────────────────
+//
+// countVisibleCells() treats UNKNOWN as an occluder, exactly like a wall. But
+// a frontier cell IS the boundary of unknown space -- searchFrontiers() only
+// promotes a cell that is knownfree AND has an unknown neighbour -- so a ray
+// arriving at one passes through the unobserved boundary layer by
+// construction. The test therefore reports "you cannot see this frontier"
+// *because* it is a frontier.
+//
+// Measured, and it is not a corner case. Of the rays cast to frontier cells in
+// a hospital leg, 67.5% were rejected on UNKNOWN against 28.4% on real
+// structure, and only 1.6% arrived clear; in the warehouse, 46.9% against
+// 42.8%, with 2.2% clear. Clusters that no viewpoint can see are retired to
+// dormant, and when only those are left the frontier set empties and FALCON
+// declares the world finished. That is why the finish amnesty, which already
+// drops the visibility bar to zero, rescues nothing: the clusters it re-offers
+// have zero measured visibility, and no bar of any height saves a cluster
+// nothing can see.
+//
+// So allow a ray to cross a BOUNDED prefix of unobserved voxels and no more.
+// The raycast runs from the frontier cell toward the viewpoint, so the
+// tolerated voxels are exactly the boundary layer around the cell; unknown
+// encountered further along the ray is a genuinely unexplored volume being
+// looked through, and still blocks. OCCUPIED always blocks, at any distance,
+// which is what keeps a sealed cavity -- the warehouse's hollow crates --
+// unviewable: a ray into one crosses the shell first.
+//
+// 0 restores upstream exactly.
+int unknownVisibilityTolerance() {
+  static bool loaded = false;
+  static int tolerance = 0;
+  if (!loaded) {
+    ros::param::param("/frontier_finder/visib_unknown_tolerance", tolerance, 0);
+    loaded = true;
+    ROS_WARN("[visib_unknown] tolerance=%d voxel(s) of unobserved space per ray "
+             "(0 restores upstream: any UNKNOWN blocks the line of sight)",
+             tolerance);
+  }
+  return tolerance;
+}
+
+
 }  // namespace
 
